# Copy to .env.local and fill from Firebase console:
# Project settings > General > Your apps > Web app > SDK setup and configuration
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# Must be the origin the app is SERVED from (gaycruisebingo.com), NOT the Firebase
# console default gaycruisebingo.firebaseapp.com. Firebase hosts the OAuth handler
# at <authDomain>/__/auth/handler; when that origin differs from where the app
# runs, storage-partitioned mobile browsers (iOS in-app webviews, Safari ITP)
# can't read the pre-redirect sign-in state and Google sign-in dies with "Unable
# to process request due to missing initial state". Same-origin avoids the split.
# Firebase Hosting uses gaycruisebingo.com; the production Vercel mirror instead
# sets gaycruisebingo.vercel.app and proxies /__/auth/* via vercel.json.
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=gaycruisebingo.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=gaycruisebingo
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=gaycruisebingo.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=849798007162
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
# Analytics > Data streams > Web > Measurement ID (G-XXXXXXX). Optional in dev.
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Which event/board this build points at — AND a build-mode switch (#543,
# docs/adr/0009-event-resolved-from-hostname.md). PRESENCE of a value marks a
# single-Event build: the bundle serves exactly this Event and never consults
# `hostnames/{host}` for Event ID or Edition. Its independent adult-posture
# watcher may still read that document (ADR 0012). Leave it EMPTY for a multi-Event /
# hostname-resolved build (Five Across wildcard hosts), or the build will
# short-circuit resolution and serve this baked event on every host it lands
# on. The legacy Gay Cruise Bingo deployment is a single-Event build:
VITE_EVENT_ID=med-2026

# Edition brand for a single-Event build (src/editions.ts): `gcb`, `vacay`, or
# `fiveacross`. Every registered deploy target names this explicitly. A hostname-resolved build (empty VITE_EVENT_ID) ignores
# this and takes its Edition from `hostnames/{host}.edition`; a single-Event
# build has no Edition lookup, so this is its ONLY Edition signal — a Vacay build that
# omits it silently ships Gay Cruise Bingo sign-in copy even with the correct
# VITE_EVENT_ID. Set the two together.
#
# It is read at BUILD time as well as at runtime: index.html's <title> and iOS
# home-screen label, and the PWA manifest's name/short_name, are all baked from
# it (#586). Changing it therefore needs a rebuild, not just a redeploy — and an
# installed PWA keeps the name it was installed under until it is reinstalled.
# The build honours it ONLY when VITE_EVENT_ID is set: a hostname-resolved build
# ignores this at build time exactly as it does at runtime, so a value left here
# by accident cannot brand a bundle that many Events share.
VITE_EDITION=gcb

# The 18+ posture seed for a single-Event build. Only the literal value `false`
# opts out. Registered targets set this explicitly; a general-audience target
# also needs a serving-host routing document that confirms that posture.
VITE_ADULT_CONTENT=true

# Optional (Phase 1): App Check reCAPTCHA Enterprise site key.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=

# PostHog client-side product analytics (runs alongside GA4). The `phc_` project
# key is client-safe/public. Leave VITE_POSTHOG_KEY blank to disable PostHog.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Ingestion host override — LEAVE UNSET (#612). The client walks an in-code
# priority-ordered failover chain (src/posthog.ts POSTHOG_INGEST_HOSTS:
# d.fiveacross.app → d.nathanpayne.com → d.gaycruisebingo.com → PostHog Cloud
# US direct), probing at boot and taking the first host that answers. Setting
# this var to a host OUTSIDE that chain silently DISABLES the failover for the
# whole session (the #540/#578 launch-handoff trap); restating a chain member
# is tolerated but pointless. Set https://us.i.posthog.com only when a
# non-production build must deliberately bypass every proxy for diagnostics.
# The PostHog UI host is fixed to https://us.posthog.com in code.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=

# --- Cloud Functions config (issue #101) -------------------------------------
# The email notifier's config (EMAIL_FROM, ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL, APP_BASE_URL, and
# the RESEND_API_KEY secret) is NOT read from this file. Firebase Functions v2
# loads params/dotenv from the functions source dir (firebase.json
# functions.source = "functions"), so those go in functions/.env — see
# functions/.env.example. Setting them here has no effect on the deployed
# functions.

# --- Centralised auth handoff (#549, ADR 0010) --------------------------------
# COMMENTED ON PURPOSE — these two are read but must not be DEFINED here.
# `scripts/build-target.mjs` requires every VITE_* key this file defines to be
# present in each target's env file, and those files (`.env.gaycruisebingo`,
# `.env.fiveacross`) are untracked operator-held state. Defining a key here
# therefore hard-fails every build and deploy until a human edits both — the
# client-side twin of the `functions/.env.<projectId>` trap in #767. Both keys
# are optional with safe in-code defaults (src/auth/authMode.ts), so leaving
# them commented costs nothing and breaks nothing.
#
# Which route sign-in takes. Unset (the default) means `handoff`: Google
# validates OAuth redirect URIs exactly, so a wildcard Event host
# (`<slug>.fiveacross.app`) can never be its own callback and sign-in has to
# happen at one central registered origin. `same_origin` is the ESCAPE HATCH —
# it refuses to leave the origin at all, which works only where the OAuth helper
# is already same-origin (the host is in FIRST_PARTY_AUTH_HOSTS in
# src/auth-domain.ts, or the build bakes VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN equal to it).
# Selecting it anywhere else fails loudly at mount rather than silently falling
# back. A misspelled value is rejected, not defaulted.
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=handoff
#
# The central auth origin the handoff bounces through. Required in handoff mode
# on any host that is not already registered; absent, sign-in there reports
# itself unavailable rather than dead-ending mid-flow. `gaycruisebingo` is a
# single registered origin that signs in same-origin and never mints a handoff,
# so its target leaves this unset. The `fiveacross` target wants
# https://auth.fiveacross.app once #547 has provisioned that host in the
# Firebase Auth authorized domains and the Google OAuth web client.
# VITE_AUTH_HANDOFF_ORIGIN=https://auth.fiveacross.app
